    "created_at": "2026-11-19T01:34:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T01:34:48Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/2600-tilted-not-judged · PR #2664 · pinned by a_tilted_slot_into_the_step_bar_is_refused, the_step_bars_wall_facets_lie_on_the_cylinder · merges when reviewed\n\nThe cause is not the tilt. A tilted operation is judged at generation (the test `a_tilted_slot_into_a_meshed_bar_is_refused` passes on unchanged main). The STEP import of the reported bar made wall facets that ran through the solid, as much as 25 mm inside the cylinder. Each gouge law then judged against a part that was too small. The PR makes the importer measure and refine these facets.\n\nNot changed: a program that the stock sim does not judge still posts on its generator verdicts, with the visible line. The second finding of the report (A0 B180 with `basis_version` 0 posts XY turned 90 degrees) is not in this PR.\n",
